 ## Overview
-Multiplex Training via S3IM is a training paradigm that combines a conventional pixel-wise loss (e.g., MSE or L1) with a Stochastic Structural SIMilarity (S3IM) loss to improve neural field reconstruction quality, particularly for complex details and sparse inputs [S1]. It sets itself apart from standard SSIM optimization by using stochastic patch sampling to capture non-local structural information from distant pixels across different images, whereas standard SSIM via local patches only captures structural information from nearby pixels within a single image [S1].
+Multiplex Training via S3IM is a training paradigm that combines a conventional pixel-wise loss (e.g., L1 or MSE) with a Stochastic Structural SIMilarity (S3IM) loss to improve neural field reconstruction quality, particularly for complex details and sparse inputs [S1]. It sets itself apart from standard SSIM optimization by using stochastic patch generation to capture non-local structural information from distant pixels across different images, whereas standard SSIM via local patches only captures structural information from nearby pixels within a single image [S1].
 
