 ### S3IM (Stochastic Structural SIMilarity)
-A loss metric that averages SSIM over $M$ stochastic patches rather than fixed local patches, enabling the capture of non-local structural information across distant pixels and different images [S1]. Choose it when standard SSIM optimization fails to capture global structure or when local patch sampling proves computationally expensive [S1]. [Link](10895-s3im-stochastic-structural-similarity.md)
-
-### NeuS
-A neural surface representation method that relates volume occupancy to density for improved geometry reconstruction [S1]. It is adapted for multiplex training by replacing the standard color loss with the multiplex color loss $L_{\mathrm{M},\mathrm{color}} = L_{\mathrm{color}} + \lambda L_{\SSSIM}$, where $L_{\mathrm{color}}$ uses an L1 form [S1]. Choose it when high-fidelity surface geometry and RGB reconstruction are required simultaneously [S1]. [Link](10895-s3im-stochastic-structural-similarity.md)
+The core loss component that uses stochastic patching to capture non-local structural information. It differs from standard SSIM by avoiding local-patch dataloaders and capturing cross-image structural dependencies.(10895-s3im-stochastic-structural-similarity.md)
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time and Memory Complexity**: The extra computational cost is limited because S3IM requires only one backpropagation per iteration, similar to standard training, despite the loop over $M$ patches [S1].
+*   **Time and Memory Complexity**: The extra computational cost is limited because S3IM requires only one backpropagation per iteration, similar to standard training [S1]. The complexity scales linearly with $M$, the number of stochastic patches.
 *   **Measured Performance**:
