 ## Background
-*   **Origin**: Introduced in the paper "S3IM: Stochastic Structural SIMilarity and Its Unreasonable Effectiveness for Neural Fields" [S1].
-*   **History**: The method is model-agnostic and orthogonal to existing point-wise training paradigms and NeRF variants like DVGO, TensoRF, D-NeRF, and NeuS [S1]. It was developed to address the limitations of standard SSIM optimization in neural field reconstruction [S1].
-*   **Usage**: Applied to NeRF, DVGO, TensoRF, D-NeRF, and NeuS [S1].
+Multiplex Training via S3IM was introduced in the paper "S3IM: Stochastic Structural SIMilarity and Its Unreasonable Effectiveness for Neural Fields" [S1]. It is model-agnostic and orthogonal to existing point-wise training paradigms and NeRF variants [S1]. It has been applied to NeRF, DVGO, TensoRF, D-NeRF, and NeuS [S1].
 
